output.formatted:
I could not find a reliable SPARQL query that returns the stepmother of Angélique de Froissy from the DBpedia endpoint for two reasons: 1) The DBpedia resource uses diacritics in IRIs (e.g. Angélique_de_Froissy, Françoise_Marie_de_Bourbon) which caused repeated encoding/parse errors when used inside executed SPARQL queries through this tool, while the list() helper could return some triples but not reliably all family relations. 2) The family relationships in DBpedia appear to be inconsistently modeled for this historical person (some relevant properties such as dbp:stepmother or dbp:stepMother did not appear for the resource in the data I could retrieve), so I couldn't find a single predicate that reliably yields the stepmother.

What I tried (summary):
- Located the Angélique de Froissy resource in DBpedia.
- Inspected available triples for that resource (dbo:abstract, labels, etc.). The abstract text indicates Angélique was the daughter of Philippe (the Duke of Orléans) and Charlotte Desmares and was legitimated in 1722.
- From historical knowledge, Philippe II, Duke of Orléans was married to Françoise-Marie de Bourbon, who would be Angélique's stepmother. However, I couldn't locate an explicit triple in DBpedia linking Angélique to Françoise-Marie via a stepmother property.

Because of these limitations I cannot produce a SPARQL query that I can both (a) run successfully against the endpoint via this tool and (b) that returns a DBpedia IRI for the stepmother with confidence. Below is my best SPARQL attempt (may fail due to IRI/diacritic handling or because the property is not present in DBpedia):

SPARQL query over dbpedia:
PREFIX dbp: <http://dbpedia.org/property/>
PREFIX dbr: <http://dbpedia.org/resource/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?stepmother ?stepmotherLabel WHERE {
  {
    dbr:Ang%C3%A9lique_de_Froissy dbp:stepmother ?stepmother .
  } UNION {
    dbr:Ang%C3%A9lique_de_Froissy dbp:stepMother ?stepmother .
  } UNION {
    dbr:Ang%C3%A9lique_de_Froissy ?p ?stepmother .
    FILTER(regex(str(?p) , "step" , "i"))
  }
  OPTIONAL {
    ?stepmother rdfs:label ?stepmotherLabel .
    FILTER(lang(?stepmotherLabel) = "en")
  }
}

Using properties:
